    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract thinking and real-world problem-solving—something I enjoy dissecting, especially when connecting it to my love for history. While the concepts can initially feel dense, once they click (like quadratic formulas or calculus), they become almost intuitive. The structure of proofs and systematic logic aligns with how I approach board games or composing music, but I admit some topics—like advanced algebra—still leave me wanting more concrete applications.",
